    },
    {
      "feature": "Milestone ledger rows already have an analogous third-disposition mechanism ('not_applicable' status + auditable notApplicableDecision {reason, decidedBy, decidedAt}) requiring an independently auditable justification, exactly the same problem class ('legitimately excluded planned item') this story solves at the checklist/binding layer",
      "covered_by": null,
      "status": "excluded",
      "excluded_by": "OQ-2 resolution (scope-check.json) + plan.md CHK-004: new withdrawn/bindingDispositions vocabulary is intentionally kept separate from MilestoneLedgerItem.notApplicableDecision because notApplicableDecision means 'never applied to this story' (a PLAN classification) while 'withdrawn' means 'planned as a real promise, then proven undeliverable' (a post-freeze correction); the auditable-decisionRef pattern is reused even though the disposition vocabulary is distinct -- a recorded, reasoned choice, not an oversight.",
      "source": "decisions:milestone-not-applicable-justification.md"
    },
    {
      "feature": "ProofStoryAcceptanceBinding.verificationTopology.applicability already has a 'not_applicable' mode plus decisionRef, and structural rule 11 already requires 'an independently auditable decision reference' for any acceptance-binding exemption -- an existing mechanism for the same concept CHK-004/CHK-005's new bindingDispositions[] independently reinvents",
      "covered_by": null,
      "status": "excluded",
      "excluded_by": "OQ-2 resolution (scope-check.json) + plan.md CHK-004: bindingDispositions[] deliberately does NOT reuse verificationTopology.applicability.mode='not_applicable' because that field lives on the binding written only by the PLAN-frozen proofstory_contract_set (allowedPhases=['PLAN']), making it unreachable from DEV/REVIEW -- exactly the constraint this story exists to remove; mutating it would also overwrite the frozen original binding F-062 requires stay byte-for-byte readable. The auditable decisionRef pattern (AT_INVALID_NA_DECISION / rule 11) is reused; the disposition vocabulary is not.",
      "source": "decisions:proofstory-acceptance-topology-and-pre-review-gates-execution-plan.md"
    }
